[[Skyrim:Hevnoraak (item)|Hevnoraak]] is an iron [[Skyrim:Dragon Priest|dragon priest]] [[Skyrim:Dragon Priest Mask|mask]] gained by killing [[Skyrim:Hevnoraak (creature)|Hevnoraak]] within the [[Skyrim:Nordic Ruins|Nordic Ruin]] of [[Skyrim:Valthume|Valthume]]. The enchantment provides poison and disease immunity for all diseases and poisons except for ones that ignore disease and poison resistance. It can be [[Skyrim:Workbench|improved]] with [[Skyrim:Iron Ingot|iron ingots]].<includeonly>

For more information, see the [[Skyrim:Hevnoraak (item)|Hevnoraak]] article.</includeonly><noinclude>
{{NewLeft}}

==Notes==
* Placing Hevnoraak on its pedestal at [[Skyrim:Bromjunaar Sanctuary|Bromjunaar Sanctuary]] will remove any bonuses that it gained from tempering.
* All dragon priest masks are considered to be circlets in terms of equipment slots, meaning that they can be worn simultaneously with some bugged items, as detailed under [[Skyrim:Circlet|circlets]].
* Hevno means "brutal" in the [[Lore:Dragon Language|dragon language]].
* [[Skyrim:Hendraheim (place)|Hendraheim]]{{CC|Hendraheim}}, [[Skyrim:Shadowfoot Sanctum (place)|Shadowfoot Sanctum]]{{CC|Shadowfoot Sanctum}}, [[Skyrim:Tundra Homestead (place)|Tundra Homestead]]'s cellar{{CC|Tundra Homestead}}, [[Skyrim:Bloodchill Manor|Bloodchill Cavern]]{{CC|Bloodchill Manor}},  and [[Skyrim:Myrwatch (place)|Myrwatch]]'s gallery{{CC|Myrwatch}} contain a special holder for this item.
*As with other equipment which provides disease immunity, Hevnoraak will protect against all diseases except those contracted by traps, as [[Skyrim:Resist Disease|detailed here]].
*Despite both the Resist Disease and Resist Poison enchantments being bright green in color (when viewed from the inventory, on other pieces), the enchantment color of Hevnoraak is red.

